From c2547e0bbb1a3812c0d557e54435f312f2bfb501 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fork <fork@localhost>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 14:54:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Serve a declared authority as the operator's own surface

A page served from a declared `trustedHosts` authority passed the /api
fence and authenticated with the process token, but the browser still
classified it as foreign because `isLoopback` was decided from the page
hostname alone. Settings, credentials, and every other privileged client
row were therefore inert on a LAN page ("settings are unavailable in this
browser"), even though the Host had admitted it.

Classify the page authority against the admitted set instead: the Host
publishes the same `trustedHosts` it fences with, and the browser half
accepts a page on one of them as its own Host. An all-interfaces bind now
needs at least one declared authority, which keeps `--host 0.0.0.0`
opt-in and explicit.
